{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0130a666-0620-4dc6-a158-7fc732cfba9c","agentId":"a2520a44972818a06","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are a skeptical, READ-ONLY code reviewer (write nothing: no files, no git changes). Review `git -C /home/sauyon/devel/dotfiles/.drovr/wt/orca-cli-skills diff 2f5d3162..HEAD` in full (orca.nix, tests/orca-cli-skills.sh, tests/sandbox-fonts.sh). Angles: security, quality/consistency, comment accuracy, and whether each test case fails on a regression of its claim. Round 5; `git log 2f5d3162..HEAD` lists earlier fixes and deliberately-left nits — don't re-raise those unless actually Important.\n\nContext: public home-manager dotfiles repo (no email addresses or private data). orca.nix: GUI `orca-ide-app` (nixGL-wrapped appimageTools.wrapType2, dieWithParent=false), CLI `orca-ide`/`orca` (buildFHSEnv, ORCA_APP_EXECUTABLE → GUI), both launchers now wrapped by a `forwardSignals` shell snippet that backgrounds bwrap and forwards TERM/HUP to its child; six Orca skills in ~/.claude/skills pinned to the app's sourceCommit. Is the code now more complex than the repo's style warrants — is there a simpler correct design (e.g. bwrap options, `--unshare-pid` + `--as-pid-1`, systemd KillMode drop-in, tini/dumb-init-style tools in nixpkgs) that should replace forwardSignals? Check nixpkgs (`nix eval --raw --impure --expr '(builtins.getFlake (toString /home/sauyon/devel/dotfiles)).inputs.nixpkgs.outPath'`, pkgs/build-support/build-fhsenv-bubblewrap) and bwrap's man page/options (`bwrap --help`). Verify comment claims. Confirm the test never prints secret env values (ORCA_AGENT_HOOK_TOKEN is in env); check the test's background process and temp-dir cleanup.\n\nRate every finding Critical / Important / nit with file:line; say explicitly when none at a severity. Final message = findings."},"uuid":"90ef60c5-98e7-4915-a130-2252fe862766","timestamp":"2026-10-24T11:07:35.190Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd"